NEWS

* Changes in 0.27.2 since 0.27.1
** Core
*** Cast functions were removed.
*** Several pre-1.13.1 M2-Planet workarounds were removed.
** Build
*** Mes now requires M2-Planet >= 1.13.1.
*** Mes is now installable as a Guix channnel:
guix time-machine \
  --channels=https://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/mes.git/tree/build-aux/channels.sh \
  -- shell mes
*** GNUmakefile supports building `.go' files directly
*** Running the test suite during bootstrap, with Gash, is now supported
*** Mes now builds with gcc-16.
** Mes
*** 6 new functions were added:
string-copy!, vector-copy!, vector-copy!, vector-fill!, vector-fill,
vector-fold-right.
** MesCC
*** MesCC now works with NYACC versions 2.02.4 and 3.00.0
*** MesCC now ignores some common options: -f*, -M*, -W*.
*** MesCC now fails early when pre-processing fails.
** Mes C Library
*** 13 prototypes were added:
clearerr, ctime, fileno, freopen, getpwnam, mktmp, rewind, setbuf
sigblock, sigemptyset, sigsetmask strdup, ttyname.
*** The v*printf and v*scanf prototypes were moved to stdio.h
** Noteworthy bug fixes
*** The build system no longer compiles each file twice
This was a tracing regression/typo introduced in v0.20
*** A bug in string-every was fixed and made more efficient.
*** A bug in define-private was fixed.
*** A workaround for a hygiene problem in `or' using `r' was added.
*** The reader now skips escaped newline characters.

